hostname r1
!
ip routing
!
interface Loopback0
   ip address 10.0.0.1/32
!
interface Ethernet1
   description to r2:eth1
   no switchport
   ip address 10.1.12.1/30
!
! ============================================================
! YOUR TASKS ON R1
! ============================================================
!
! TASK 1 — Base BGP session
!   configure
!   router bgp 65001
!      bgp router-id 10.0.0.1
!      neighbor 10.1.12.2 remote-as 65002
!      !
!      address-family ipv4
!         neighbor 10.1.12.2 activate
!         network 10.0.0.1/32
!      !
!
! TASK 2 — Attach a standard community to your loopback advertisement
!   Create a route-map that sets community 65001:100 on outbound updates.
!   Apply it with: neighbor 10.1.12.2 route-map SET-COMM out
!
!   ip community-list standard MY-ORIGIN permit 65001:100
!
!   route-map SET-COMM permit 10
!      set community 65001:100
!
!   Then inside address-family ipv4:
!      neighbor 10.1.12.2 send-community
!      neighbor 10.1.12.2 route-map SET-COMM out
!
!   Verify on r2: show bgp ipv4 unicast 10.0.0.1/32
!   Look for "Community: 65001:100" in the output.
!
! NOTE: In EOS, you MUST explicitly configure "neighbor X send-community" for
!   standard communities on eBGP sessions. They are NOT sent automatically.
!
! TASK 3 — Well-known community: no-export
!   The no-export community tells r2: "accept this route but do NOT
!   advertise it to any eBGP peer (r3)."
!
!   Modify SET-COMM to set community no-export instead of (or in addition to) 65001:100:
!   route-map SET-COMM permit 10
!      set community no-export
!
!   Verify: after applying, r3 should NOT have 10.0.0.1/32 in its table.
!   Check on r3: show bgp ipv4 unicast
!
! TASK 4 — Well-known community: no-advertise
!   Similar to no-export but stronger: r2 will not advertise to ANY
!   neighbor (including iBGP). The route stays only in r2's local RIB.
!
!   route-map SET-COMM permit 10
!      set community no-advertise
!
! TASK 5 — Combining communities
!   You can set multiple communities at once:
!   route-map SET-COMM permit 10
!      set community 65001:100 65001:200 no-export additive
!
!   The "additive" keyword appends instead of replacing communities.
! ============================================================
end
